                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/12–149</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation, by the Director of
                        the Office of Chinese Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Sprouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-12-01">December 1, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Graves telephoned this morning and, speaking in guarded fashion, said that
                    his Embassy had been directed by the Foreign Office to inform the Department
                    that Mr. Bevin planned to present to the Cabinet for decision during the week of
                    December 12–19 the question of the date on which the British Government would
                    extend recognition to the Chinese Communist regime. He said that the Foreign
                    Office would continue to keep the Department fully informed of all developments
                    in this regard.</p>
            </div>
